# Environment variables for Crema.
#
# They live in three different places. Only section 1 goes in .env.local;
# the others are listed here so everything is in one spot.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. .env.local: read by Next.js and the Convex CLI
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# You normally don't write these by hand: the first `bun run dev` (or
# `bunx convex dev`) logs you in to Convex, creates or picks a dev deployment,
# and writes them to .env.local.

# The Convex dev deployment that `convex dev` pushes to.
CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=dev:your-deployment-name

# The deployment's URL. Used by the browser and the Next.js server
# (src/lib/convexAuth.tsx, src/lib/serverAuth.ts).
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL=https://your-deployment-name.convex.cloud

# `convex dev` also writes NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_SITE_URL (the HTTP-actions URL).
# The app doesn't use it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Convex deployment environment: NOT read from .env files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by the Convex functions (convex/convex.config.ts, convex/auth.ts). Set
# them per deployment in the Convex dashboard (Settings → Environment Variables)
# or with:
#   bunx convex env set AUTH_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID 1234-abc.apps.googleusercontent.com
#   (add --prod for the production deployment)
#
# Google sign-in. Required on every deployment: the backend won't deploy without
# them. Create a "Web application" OAuth client in the Google Cloud console and
# add <CONVEX_SITE_URL>/oauth/google/callback as an authorized redirect URI
# (`bunx convex env get CONVEX_SITE_URL` prints the site URL). README → Step 3.
#
# AUTH_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=1234-abc.apps.googleusercontent.com
# AUTH_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=GOCSPX-...
#
# Where Google sign-in may send people back to: full origin(s) with scheme,
# no trailing slash, comma-separated. Defaults to http://localhost:3000.
#
# SITE_ORIGIN=https://crema.vercel.app,http://localhost:3000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Vercel project settings: build time only
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A production deploy key from the Convex dashboard (Settings → Deploy keys).
# The build (see vercel.json) uses it to deploy the Convex functions and to set
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL to the production deployment.
#
# CONVEX_DEPLOY_KEY=prod:your-deployment-name|...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Browser used by scripts/shoot.ts (headless screenshots for agents).
# Defaults to Microsoft Edge's standard install path on Windows.
#
# BROWSER=C:/Program Files (x86)/Microsoft/Edge/Application/msedge.exe
